   "source": [
    "{\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Evaluation of the hierarchy attribute extraction pipeline\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Here we evaluate the performance of **Step 2** of the Ariadne pipeline: extracting SNOMED CT hierarchy attributes for medical terms.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The pipeline:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. Retrieves similar reference SNOMED terms (few-shot examples)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. Uses an LLM to extract attribute components from the medical term\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. Retrieves candidate concepts for each extracted component via vector search\\n\",\n",
    "    \"4. Uses an LLM to select the best candidate for each attribute\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Setup\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Before running this notebook, make sure the environment is set up as described in the README.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This includes:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Credentials for a database with the OHDSI Vocabulary loaded (including `snomed_attribute` and `snomed_reference` tables)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"  If you need to recreate these two tables, please run /sandbox/build_pg_indexes_attributes.py\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Credentials for the LLM API\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- A `config_condition_mapping.yaml` with the hierarchy prompts configured\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"All results will be stored in the `data/notebook_results` folder.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Most code blocks will load results from file if they already exist, to save time and costs.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Delete those files to rerun the corresponding steps.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": []\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Configuration\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Load the hierarchy pipeline configuration from `config_condition_mapping.yaml`.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"import json\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import os\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from pathlib import Path\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import pandas as pd\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from dotenv import load_dotenv\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"project_root = Path.cwd().parent.parent\\n\",\n",
    "    \"load_dotenv()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from ariadne.utils.config import load_hierarchy_settings\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"cfg = load_hierarchy_settings(str(project_root / \\\"config_condition_mapping.yaml\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Extraction model: {cfg.models.extraction}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Selection model: {cfg.models.selection}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Reference examples: {cfg.retrieval.num_reference_examples}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Top-k per category: {cfg.retrieval.top_k_per_category}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Gold standard\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"We use the hierarchy attributes gold standard file.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Each row maps a source concept to an expected SNOMED attribute (e.g. finding site, associated morphology).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This gold standard contains the following columns:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `concept_id_1`: the concept ID of the source term\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `concept_name_1`: the source term text\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `concept_id_2`: the concept ID of the expected attribute value (e.g. a finding site concept)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `concept_code_2`: the concept code of the expected attribute value (e.g. a finding site concept)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `concept_name_2`: the name of the expected attribute value\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `attribute_category`: the SNOMED relationship type (e.g. `Has finding site`, `Has asso morph`, `Has causative agent`)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"attribute_gs_path = project_root / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"gold_standards\\\" / \\\"hierarchy_attributes_snomed_gs.csv\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Alternative: use unmatched terms from the exact matching pipeline (Step 1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# attribute_gs_path = project_root / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"notebook_results\\\" / \\\"exact_matching_vector_search_results.csv\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"attribute_gs = pd.read_csv(attribute_gs_path)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# If using exact_matching_vector_search_results.csv, filter to unmatched terms only:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# attribute_gs = attribute_gs[attribute_gs[\\\"mapped_concept_id\\\"] == -1]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Attribute GS: {len(attribute_gs)} rows\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"unique_terms = attribute_gs[[\\\"concept_id_1\\\", \\\"concept_name_1\\\"]].drop_duplicates()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Unique terms: {len(unique_terms)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"attribute_gs.head(10)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Run the hierarchy attribute extraction pipeline\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"We use `process_gold_standard` from the evaluator module, which:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. Iterates over each unique term in the gold standard\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. Runs the four-step attribute extraction pipeline (`find_attributes_two_stage`)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. Supports checkpointing (resumes from where it left off if interrupted)\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"import logging\\n\",\n",
    "    \"logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format=\\\"%(asctime)s  %(message)s\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from ariadne.hierarchy.evaluator import process_gold_standard\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from ariadne.hierarchy.evaluator import _build_prediction_rows\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from ariadne.hierarchy.searchers import SnomedAttributeSearcher, SnomedReferenceSearcher\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"raw_results_file = project_root / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"notebook_results\\\" / \\\"hierarchy_results_raw.json\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if raw_results_file.exists():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    with open(raw_results_file, \\\"r\\\") as f:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        results = json.load(f)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"Loaded {len(results)} cached results from file.\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Exclude gold standard terms from reference examples to prevent data leakage\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    gs_concept_ids = set(attribute_gs[\\\"concept_id_1\\\"].unique())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    with SnomedAttributeSearcher(cfg=cfg) as attr_idx, \\\\\\n\",\n",
    "    \"         SnomedReferenceSearcher(cfg=cfg, exclude_concept_ids=gs_concept_ids) as ref_idx:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        results = process_gold_standard(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            str(attribute_gs_path),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            attr_idx,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            reference_index=ref_idx,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            cfg=cfg,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            max_workers=8,  \\n\",\n",
    "    \"        )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Save raw results for debugging\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    with open(raw_results_file, \\\"w\\\") as f:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        json.dump(results, f, indent=2, default=str)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"Processed {len(results)} terms. Results saved.\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"total_cost = sum(r.get(\\\"cost\\\", {}).get(\\\"total_cost\\\", 0.0) for r in results if \\\"cost\\\" in r)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Total API cost: ${total_cost:.4f}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Save flat predictions CSV (one row per attribute) — input for RF2 export\\n\",\n",
    "    \"results_df = pd.DataFrame(_build_prediction_rows(results))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"results_df.to_csv(project_root / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"notebook_results\\\" / \\\"attribute_results.csv\\\", index=False)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Saved {len(results_df)} attribute rows to attribute_results.csv\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Columns: {results_df.columns.tolist()}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"results_df.head(10)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Evaluation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"We evaluate the pipeline results against the gold standard using a full outer join.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Each predicted attribute is matched against the expected attribute by `(concept_id_1, concept_id_2, attribute_category)`.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This gives us precision, recall, and F1 scores.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"from ariadne.hierarchy.evaluator import evaluate_results\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Set output directory relative to project root\\n\",\n",
    "    \"cfg.evaluation.output_dir = str(project_root / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"notebook_results\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"eval_df = evaluate_results(results, str(attribute_gs_path), cfg=cfg)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"eval_df.head(20)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Per-category breakdown\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"n_match = (eval_df[\\\"status\\\"] == \\\"match\\\").sum()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"n_missed = (eval_df[\\\"status\\\"] == \\\"missed\\\").sum()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"n_extra = (eval_df[\\\"status\\\"] == \\\"extra\\\").sum()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"n_gs = n_match + n_missed\\n\",\n",
    "    \"n_pred = n_match + n_extra\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"precision = n_match / n_pred * 100 if n_pred else 0.0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"recall = n_match / n_gs * 100 if n_gs else 0.0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"f1 = 2 * precision * recall / (precision + recall) if (precision + recall) else 0.0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Gold standard rows: {n_gs}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Predicted rows:     {n_pred}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Matched:            {n_match}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Precision:          {precision:.1f}%\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Recall:             {recall:.1f}%\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"F1:                 {f1:.1f}%\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"breakdown = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    eval_df.groupby(\\\"attribute_category\\\")[\\\"status\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .value_counts()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .unstack(fill_value=0)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .reindex(columns=[\\\"match\\\", \\\"missed\\\", \\\"extra\\\"], fill_value=0)\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"breakdown[\\\"precision%\\\"] = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    breakdown[\\\"match\\\"] / (breakdown[\\\"match\\\"] + breakdown[\\\"extra\\\"]).clip(lower=1) * 100\\n\",\n",
    "    \").round(1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"breakdown[\\\"recall%\\\"] = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    breakdown[\\\"match\\\"] / (breakdown[\\\"match\\\"] + breakdown[\\\"missed\\\"]).clip(lower=1) * 100\\n\",\n",
    "    \").round(1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"breakdown\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Missed and extra predictions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Inspect which attributes were missed by the pipeline and which were incorrectly predicted.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"missed = eval_df[eval_df[\\\"status\\\"] == \\\"missed\\\"][[\\\"concept_id_1\\\", \\\"concept_name_1\\\", \\\"attribute_category\\\", \\\"gs_concept_name_2\\\"]]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Missed predictions: {len(missed)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"extra = eval_df[eval_df[\\\"status\\\"] == \\\"extra\\\"][[\\\"concept_id_1\\\", \\\"concept_name_1\\\", \\\"attribute_category\\\", \\\"predicted_concept_name_2\\\"]]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Extra predictions: {len(extra)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"joined = missed.merge(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    extra,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    on=[\\\"concept_id_1\\\", \\\"concept_name_1\\\", \\\"attribute_category\\\"],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    how=\\\"outer\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    suffixes=(\\\"_missed\\\", \\\"_extra\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    indicator=True\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"joined.head(20)\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## RF2 Delta Export\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Convert the predicted attributes to SNOMED CT RF2 delta files for use with the ELK reasoner.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Source OMOP concept IDs are remapped to synthetic SCTIDs (starting at 1 000 000 001)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"to avoid collisions with real SNOMED IDs in the base release.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Concept definitions are expressed as **OWL Functional Syntax axioms** in the OWL Axiom Reference Set,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"which gives ELK more precise subsumption semantics than the legacy StatedRelationship format:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- A concept with attributes becomes `EquivalentClasses(:src ObjectIntersectionOf(:parent ObjectSomeValuesFrom(:609096000 ...)))`\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- A concept with no attributes falls back to `SubClassOf(:src :parent)`\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The output ZIP contains files under `Delta/`:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `Delta/Terminology/sct2_Concept_Delta_INT_{date}.txt` — one row per source term (sufficiently defined)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `Delta/Terminology/sct2_StatedRelationship_Delta_INT_{date}.txt` — header-only placeholder\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `Delta/Terminology/sct2_Relationship_Delta_INT_{date}.txt` — header-only placeholder (required by toolkit)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `Delta/Refset/Content/der2_sRefset_OWLAxiomDelta_INT_{date}.txt` — OWL axiom per source concept\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `Delta/Refset/Metadata/der2_ssRefset_ModuleDependencyDelta_INT_{date}.txt` — module dependency\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# ── Stated parent selection via reference-term neighbourhood voting ────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import importlib\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import json\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import psycopg\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import ariadne.hierarchy.parent_selector as _ps_mod\\n\",\n",
    "    \"importlib.reload(_ps_mod)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from ariadne.hierarchy.parent_selector import build_stated_parents_map\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from ariadne.utils.utils import get_environment_variable\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"conn_str = get_environment_variable(\\\"VOCAB_CONNECTION_STRING\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"conn_str = conn_str.replace(\\\"+psycopg\\\", \\\"\\\").replace(\\\"+psycopg2\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"schema = get_environment_variable(\\\"VOCAB_SCHEMA\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Load raw hierarchy results (contains reference_examples with concept_id + similarity)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"raw_results_path = project_root / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"notebook_results\\\" / \\\"hierarchy_results_raw.json\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"with open(raw_results_path) as fh:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    raw_results = json.load(fh)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Loaded {len(raw_results)} raw result entries.\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# ── Tuning parameters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#   top_k=1: single best parent (reduces ancestor-explosion false positives)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#   min_similarity=0.7: minimum cosine similarity to count a reference term\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#   use_attr_filter=True: skip reference terms less specific than the source\\n\",\n",
    "    \"PARENT_TOP_K = 2\\n\",\n",
    "    \"PARENT_MIN_SIM = 0.6\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"with psycopg.connect(conn_str) as parent_conn:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stated_parents_map = build_stated_parents_map(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        raw_results,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        parent_conn,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        schema,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        top_k=PARENT_TOP_K,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        min_similarity=PARENT_MIN_SIM,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        use_attr_filter=True,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Coverage report\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fallback = [v for v in stated_parents_map.values() if v == [\\\"404684003\\\"]]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"specific = len(stated_parents_map) - len(fallback)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"\\\\nStated parent coverage (top_k={PARENT_TOP_K}, min_sim={PARENT_MIN_SIM}):\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"  Concepts with specific parent(s) : {specific}/{len(stated_parents_map)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"  Fell back to Clinical finding    : {len(fallback)}/{len(stated_parents_map)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Sample 5 concepts with their selected parents\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sample_ids = list(stated_parents_map)[:5]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for cid in sample_ids:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    src_name = next((e.get(\\\"source_concept_name\\\",\\\"?\\\") for e in raw_results\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                     if e.get(\\\"source_concept_id\\\") == cid), \\\"?\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  {src_name!r:50s} → {stated_parents_map[cid]}\\\")\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"import importlib, sys, shutil\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Force a fresh import — drop ALL ariadne.hierarchy modules from cache\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for mod_name in list(sys.modules.keys()):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if mod_name.startswith(\\\"ariadne\\\"):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        del sys.modules[mod_name]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from ariadne.hierarchy.rf2_exporter import export_to_rf2\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"rf2_output_dir = project_root / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"rf2_output\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Clean previous delta files to avoid stale artifacts\\n\",\n",
    "    \"old_delta = rf2_output_dir / \\\"SnomedCT_YourDelta\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if old_delta.exists():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    shutil.rmtree(old_delta)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"old_delta2 = rf2_output_dir / \\\"Delta\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if old_delta2.exists():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    shutil.rmtree(old_delta2)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"zip_path, id_map = export_to_rf2(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    source=project_root / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"notebook_results\\\" / \\\"attribute_results.csv\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    output_dir=rf2_output_dir,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stated_parent=stated_parents_map,   # per-concept parents from neighbourhood voting\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"RF2 delta written to: {zip_path}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"ID mapping: {len(id_map)} concepts (OMOP → synthetic)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Verify OWL content inline\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import zipfile\\n\",\n",
    "    \"with zipfile.ZipFile(zip_path) as zf:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    owl_name = next(n for n in zf.namelist() if \\\"OWLAxiom\\\" in n)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    with zf.open(owl_name) as f:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        owl_lines = f.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\").splitlines()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"OWL axiom rows: {len(owl_lines) - 1}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if owl_lines[1:]:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    sample = owl_lines[1].split(\\\"\\\\t\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"Sample expression: {sample[-1][:150]}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"id_map.head()\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## SNOMED Classification (ELK Reasoner)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Run the ELK OWL EL++ classifier (via [snomed-owl-toolkit](https://github.com/IHTSDO/snomed-owl-toolkit))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"to infer **Is a** (parent) relationships from the predicted attributes.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The classifier takes the RF2 delta ZIP produced above and a base SNOMED CT International Edition\\n\",\n",
    "    \"snapshot, converts both to OWL, runs ELK, and returns the inferred parent relationships.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Prerequisites\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Java 17+** installed and on PATH\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **snomed-owl-toolkit JAR** — download from [GitHub releases](https://github.com/IHTSDO/snomed-owl-toolkit/releases)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **SNOMED CT International Edition RF2 snapshot** — obtain from [MLDS](https://mlds.ihtsdotools.org/)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Pre-classification validation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Check the RF2 delta for structural issues before sending it to the classifier.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"from ariadne.hierarchy.classifier import (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    classify_delta,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    classification_summary,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    parse_classification_results,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    pre_classification_checks,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    resolve_parent_names,\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"delta_zip = project_root / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"rf2_output\\\" / next(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    f.name for f in (project_root / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"rf2_output\\\").iterdir()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if f.name.startswith(\\\"snomed_delta_\\\") and f.name.endswith(\\\".zip\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Delta ZIP: {delta_zip}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"issues = pre_classification_checks(delta_zip)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if issues:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"⚠️  Issues found:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for issue in issues:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(f\\\"  - {issue}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"✅ All pre-classification checks passed.\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Run classification\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This step takes ~90-120 seconds (dominated by loading the base SNOMED release).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The snomed-owl-toolkit converts RF2 → OWL, runs ELK, and produces a results ZIP\\n\",\n",
    "    \"with the inferred \\\"Is a\\\" relationships.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"results_zip = classify_delta(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    delta_zip,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    base_snomed_zip=str(project_root / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"SnomedCT_InternationalRF2.zip\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    toolkit_jar=str(project_root / \\\"tools\\\" / \\\"snomed-owl-toolkit-5.3.0-executable.jar\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    output_dir=project_root / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"rf2_output\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Classification results: {results_zip}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Parse results and resolve names\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Extract the new inferred \\\"Is a\\\" relationships and resolve SNOMED concept names.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"new_is_a, removed, equiv_df = parse_classification_results(results_zip)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"New inferred 'Is a' relationships: {len(new_is_a)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Redundant relationships removed:   {len(removed)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Equivalent concept rows:           {len(equiv_df)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Build lookup structures\\n\",\n",
    "    \"synth_to_omop = dict(zip(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    id_map[\\\"synthetic_sctid\\\"].astype(str),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    id_map[\\\"omop_concept_id\\\"].astype(str),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"synth_ids = set(id_map[\\\"synthetic_sctid\\\"].astype(str))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# src_name_map: OMOP ID → concept name (from id_map + attribute_gs override)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"src_name_map = {}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for _, m in id_map.iterrows():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    omop_str = str(m[\\\"omop_concept_id\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if str(m.get(\\\"concept_name\\\", \\\"\\\")):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        src_name_map[omop_str] = str(m[\\\"concept_name\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for _, gs_row in attribute_gs.iterrows():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    src_name_map[str(gs_row[\\\"concept_id_1\\\"])] = gs_row[\\\"concept_name_1\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Collect all real SCTIDs that appear as ELK results (parents or children)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"real_sctids = set()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for _, row in new_is_a.iterrows():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    src, dest = str(row[\\\"sourceId\\\"]), str(row[\\\"destinationId\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    src_is_synth = src in synth_ids\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    dest_is_synth = dest in synth_ids\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if src_is_synth and not dest_is_synth:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        real_sctids.add(dest)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    elif not src_is_synth and dest_is_synth:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        real_sctids.add(src)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Resolve SCTID → concept_name for display (keep SCTID as the ID)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sctid_name_map: dict[str, str] = {}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if real_sctids:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    with psycopg.connect(conn_str) as conn:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        with conn.cursor() as cur:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            cur.execute(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                f\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                SELECT concept_code, concept_name\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                FROM {schema}.concept\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                WHERE vocabulary_id = 'SNOMED'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                  AND concept_code = ANY(%s)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                \\\"\\\"\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                (list(real_sctids),),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            for code, name in cur.fetchall():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                sctid_name_map[str(code)] = name\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"unmapped = real_sctids - set(sctid_name_map)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if unmapped:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"{len(unmapped)} SCTIDs not found in CONCEPT table (will keep SCTID as fallback)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Build equivalence pairs from the ELK equivalences refset\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Group by mapTarget UUID — concepts sharing the same group are equivalent\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from collections import defaultdict\\n\",\n",
    "    \"equiv_groups: dict[str, list[str]] = defaultdict(list)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for _, row in equiv_df.iterrows():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    sctid = str(row[\\\"referencedComponentId\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    group = str(row[\\\"mapTarget\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    equiv_groups[group].append(sctid)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Generate \\\"Maps to\\\" pairs from equivalence groups (all pairwise within group)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"equiv_pairs_set: set[tuple[str, str]] = set()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for group_members in equiv_groups.values():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Only keep pairs where at least one member is a synthetic (delta) concept\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    synth_members = [m for m in group_members if m in synth_ids]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if not synth_members:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        continue\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for i, a in enumerate(group_members):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        for b in group_members[i+1:]:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            if a in synth_ids or b in synth_ids:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                equiv_pairs_set.add((min(a, b), max(a, b)))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Equivalence groups: {len(equiv_groups)}, pairs involving delta concepts: {len(equiv_pairs_set)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Build parents_df\\n\",\n",
    "    \"rows = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"skipped_base_only = 0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for _, row in new_is_a.iterrows():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    src, dest = str(row[\\\"sourceId\\\"]), str(row[\\\"destinationId\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    src_is_synth = src in synth_ids\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    dest_is_synth = dest in synth_ids\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if src_is_synth and dest_is_synth:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        continue  # inter-delta hierarchy handled via equivalences\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if not src_is_synth and not dest_is_synth:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        skipped_base_only += 1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        continue\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if src_is_synth and not dest_is_synth:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        omop_id = synth_to_omop[src]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        rows.append({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_id_1\\\":   omop_id,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_name_1\\\": src_name_map.get(omop_id, omop_id),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"relationship_id\\\": \\\"Is a\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_code_2\\\": dest,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_name_2\\\": sctid_name_map.get(dest, dest),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        })\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        omop_id = synth_to_omop[dest]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        rows.append({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_id_1\\\":   omop_id,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_name_1\\\": src_name_map.get(omop_id, omop_id),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"relationship_id\\\": \\\"Subsumes\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_code_2\\\": src,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_name_2\\\": sctid_name_map.get(src, src),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        })\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Add equivalent pairs as \\\"Maps to\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for a, b in equiv_pairs_set:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    a_is_synth = a in synth_ids\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    b_is_synth = b in synth_ids\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if a_is_synth and b_is_synth:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        # Both are delta concepts → use OMOP IDs\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        omop_a = synth_to_omop[a]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        omop_b = synth_to_omop[b]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        rows.append({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_id_1\\\":   omop_a,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_name_1\\\": src_name_map.get(omop_a, omop_a),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"relationship_id\\\": \\\"Maps to\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_code_2\\\": omop_b,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_name_2\\\": src_name_map.get(omop_b, omop_b),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        })\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    elif a_is_synth:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        # a is delta, b is real SNOMED\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        omop_a = synth_to_omop[a]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        rows.append({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_id_1\\\":   omop_a,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_name_1\\\": src_name_map.get(omop_a, omop_a),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"relationship_id\\\": \\\"Maps to\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_code_2\\\": b,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_name_2\\\": sctid_name_map.get(b, b),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        })\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        # b is delta, a is real SNOMED\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        omop_b = synth_to_omop[b]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        rows.append({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_id_1\\\":   omop_b,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_name_1\\\": src_name_map.get(omop_b, omop_b),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"relationship_id\\\": \\\"Maps to\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_code_2\\\": a,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"concept_name_2\\\": sctid_name_map.get(a, a),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        })\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"parents_df = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=[\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"concept_id_1\\\", \\\"concept_name_1\\\", \\\"relationship_id\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"concept_code_2\\\", \\\"concept_name_2\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"parents_csv = project_root / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"notebook_results\\\" / \\\"classification_parents.csv\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"parents_df.to_csv(parents_csv, index=False)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"n_maps_to = (parents_df[\\\"relationship_id\\\"] == \\\"Maps to\\\").sum()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Saved {len(parents_df)} parent relationships → classification_parents.csv\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"  'Is a'     : {(parents_df['relationship_id']=='Is a').sum()}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"  'Subsumes' : {(parents_df['relationship_id']=='Subsumes').sum()}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"  'Maps to'  : {n_maps_to}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"parents_df.head(20)\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Evaluation: inferred parents vs parent gold standard\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Compare the ELK-inferred \\\"Is a\\\" parents against the actual direct \\\"Is a\\\" relationships\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from the parent gold standard (`hierarchy_snomed_gs.csv`)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# ── Evaluation: concept-level breakdown ────────────────────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# For each source concept, determine the outcome:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#   - \\\"Maps to\\\":  equivalent to an existing SNOMED concept (exact match via ELK)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#   - \\\"Is a\\\":     correctly placed under a GS parent (concept_code_2 matches GS)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#   - \\\"Subsumes\\\": correctly subsumes a real SNOMED concept (concept_code_2 matches GS)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"parent_gs_path = project_root / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"gold_standards\\\" / \\\"hierarchy_snomed_gs.csv\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"parent_gs = pd.read_csv(parent_gs_path, dtype={\\\"concept_code_2\\\": str})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Ensure consistent types for join keys\\n\",\n",
    "    \"parent_gs[\\\"concept_id_1\\\"] = parent_gs[\\\"concept_id_1\\\"].astype(str)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"parent_gs[\\\"concept_code_2\\\"] = parent_gs[\\\"concept_code_2\\\"].astype(str)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"source_ids = set(str(s) for s in attribute_gs[\\\"concept_id_1\\\"].unique())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"total_source = len(source_ids)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# GS set: (concept_id_1, concept_code_2)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"actual_gs = parent_gs[parent_gs[\\\"concept_id_1\\\"].isin(source_ids)]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"actual_set = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    (r[\\\"concept_id_1\\\"], r[\\\"concept_code_2\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for _, r in actual_gs.iterrows()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Actual 'Is a' pairs from GS : {len(actual_set)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# ── Ensure parents_df keys are strings too ────────────────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"parents_df[\\\"concept_id_1\\\"] = parents_df[\\\"concept_id_1\\\"].astype(str)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"parents_df[\\\"concept_code_2\\\"] = parents_df[\\\"concept_code_2\\\"].astype(str)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# ── Per-relationship-type sets of source concepts ─────────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Concepts with \\\"Maps to\\\" (equivalent to existing SNOMED)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"maps_to_df = parents_df[parents_df[\\\"relationship_id\\\"] == \\\"Maps to\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"maps_to_concepts = set(maps_to_df[\\\"concept_id_1\\\"]) & source_ids\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Concepts with \\\"Is a\\\" where predicted parent matches GS\\n\",\n",
    "    \"is_a_df = parents_df[parents_df[\\\"relationship_id\\\"] == \\\"Is a\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"predicted_is_a = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    (row[\\\"concept_id_1\\\"], row[\\\"concept_code_2\\\"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for _, row in is_a_df.iterrows()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"is_a_correct = predicted_is_a & actual_set\\n\",\n",
    "    \"is_a_correct_concepts = {sid for sid, _ in is_a_correct}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Concepts with \\\"Subsumes\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"subsumes_df = parents_df[parents_df[\\\"relationship_id\\\"] == \\\"Subsumes\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"subsumes_concepts = set(subsumes_df[\\\"concept_id_1\\\"]) & source_ids\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# All predicted \\\"Is a\\\" source concepts (regardless of correctness)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"is_a_all_concepts = set(is_a_df[\\\"concept_id_1\\\"]) & source_ids\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# ── Print concept-level summary ───────────────────────────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"\\\\n{'Category':<45s} {'Count':>6s} {'%':>7s}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"-\\\" * 60)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"{'Total source concepts':<45s} {total_source:>6d} {'100.0%':>7s}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"{'Maps to (equivalent to existing SNOMED)':<45s} {len(maps_to_concepts):>6d} {len(maps_to_concepts)/total_source*100:>6.1f}%\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"{'Is a — matches GS parent (same code)':<45s} {len(is_a_correct_concepts):>6d} {len(is_a_correct_concepts)/total_source*100:>6.1f}%\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"{'Is a — any predicted parent':<45s} {len(is_a_all_concepts):>6d} {len(is_a_all_concepts)/total_source*100:>6.1f}%\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"{'Subsumes (subsumes a real SNOMED concept)':<45s} {len(subsumes_concepts):>6d} {len(subsumes_concepts)/total_source*100:>6.1f}%\\\")\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  }\n",
    " ],\n",
